※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4392
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4392 LANG_CONSTINIT_HOLDS_WHAT_CHANGES

※ A `constinit` variable holds nothing that can change without the variable
※ being written.  A field written `mut` is changed through its own mark and
※ not through the variable -- assigning it asks the field, not the name -- so
※ a change after the initializer would be refused by nothing and would write
※ what the entry point had made read-only.  A set or a dictionary whose
※ entries may change is the same, changed through its type.

let std := ⎕import("std")

type Counter = mut n : u32

fn counter(from: u64) → Counter:
    Counter(.n ← ⎕narrow(from, ⌜u32⌝) ?? 0u32)

constinit let counted: Counter = counter(⎕auxv(6) ?? 0u64)

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    ⎕narrow(counted.n, ⌜u6⌝) ?? 0u6
